a N-terminal cytoplasmic domain) with UBE2Q1 (via N-terminus); the interaction is direct (By similarity).SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Colocalizes with MGAT3 and ST6GAL1 in the Golgi stacks of cisternaee, including the cis-part of the Golgi stacks.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Found in trans cisternae of Golgi but is mainly localized at the plasma membrane (PubMed:1714903). B4GALT1 cell surface expression is regulated by UBE2Q1 (By similarity).SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Found in trans cisternae of Golgi.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Soluble form found in body fluids.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Ubiquitously expressed, but at very low levels in fetal and adult brain.PTM The soluble form derives from the membrane forms by proteolytic processing.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE Disease susceptibility may be associated with variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 7 family.ONLINE INFORMATION Beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 1" />
